hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1458","Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Al-Hasan bin Muslim told me, On the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “I witnessed the breaking of the fast prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr, Omar, and Uthman. They all prayed it before the sermon, and then the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descended, and it was as if I could see him sitting the men with his hand, then he came forward. He pushed them through his path until he came to the women, with Bilal with him, so he recited: O Prophet, when the believing women come to you, they will pledge their allegiance to you. Surat Al-Mumtahana, verse 12, until he concluded the verse, then he said When he finished: Are you upset about that? One woman said: No one else answered him. Al-Hasan did not know who she was: Yes. He said: So they gave in charity. He said: So he spread out. Bilal his garment, so he said: Come, may I ransom yourselves, so they began to throw the separator and the rings into Bilal’s garment.”"
